IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lga-rates`
IMPORT `lga-qa`

-- Local Government Act 1995 (WA), Part 6 Division 6 -- cases for the Q&A layer (lga-qa.l4): every exported question,
-- for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the answer
-- must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation ("it is an assumed term").
-- Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value under which the situation does
-- not hold, every later input ASSUMEd. For the owner (the baseline's seat), cases check that the answer equals the
-- baseline export's on the same facts; values are also worked by hand from the deposited text. Valuations, rates in the
-- dollar, charges and interest rates are illustrative.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked kind of land` IS A `What my land is`
ASSUME `an unasked determination` IS A `The Minister's determination for my land`
ASSUME `an unasked complaint` IS A `My complaint`
ASSUME `an unasked position on unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates`
ASSUME `an unasked objection` IS A `My objection`
ASSUME `an unasked length of year` IS A `Days in the financial year`

`as the owner` MEANS `I own land in a local government district`
`as the tenant` MEANS `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns`

`nothing overdue` MEANS `none of my rates is unpaid after its due date`
`some overdue` MEANS `some of my rates are unpaid after their due date`
`possession taken` MEANS `the local government has taken possession of my land for unpaid rates`

`not objected` MEANS `I have not objected to the rate record`
`objection pending` MEANS `I have objected, and my objection has not yet been decided`
`objection decided` MEANS `the local government has decided my objection`

§§ `The owner`

§§§ `s 6.26, s 6.53`

#ASSERT `Is the land I own rateable` `as the owner` `a privately owned home` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the land I own rateable` `as the owner` `land used exclusively for charitable purposes` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the land I own rateable` `as the owner` `a privately owned vacant lot` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my land rateable` `a privately owned vacant lot`)
#ASSERT `Is the land I own rateable` `as the tenant` `an unasked kind of land` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- $3 650 a year, rateable for 146 of 365 days: $1 460 (s 6.53(c)).
#ASSERT `How much of the year's rates must I pay now my land has become rateable` `as the owner` TRUE 3650 146 `365 days` EQUALS amount 1460
#ASSERT `How much of the year's rates must I pay now my land has become rateable` `as the owner` TRUE 3650 146 `365 days` EQUALS amount (`How much of the year's rates must I pay for land that became rateable` 3650 146 365)
-- a leap year: 3660 x 146 / 366
#ASSERT `How much of the year's rates must I pay now my land has become rateable` `as the owner` TRUE 3660 146 `366 days, as it includes 29 February` EQUALS amount 1460
#ASSERT `How much of the year's rates must I pay now my land has become rateable` `as the owner` TRUE 3660 146 `366 days, as it includes 29 February` EQUALS amount (`How much of the year's rates must I pay for land that became rateable` 3660 146 366)
#ASSERT `How much of the year's rates must I pay now my land has become rateable` `as the owner` FALSE `an unasked number` `an unasked number` `an unasked length of year` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `How much of the year's rates must I pay now my land has become rateable` `as the tenant` `an unasked fact` `an unasked number` `an unasked number` `an unasked length of year` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

