§§§ `Subdivision 7`

-- A valuation complaint goes under the Valuation of Land Act 1978 (s 6.80), and differential rates are not read.
#ASSERT `Where does my complaint about my rates go to` `as the owner` `my valuation is too high` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `the complaint goes to` `an objection under the Valuation of Land Act 1978, not this Act (s 6.80)`
#ASSERT `Where does my complaint about my rates go to` `as the owner` `the rate record gives my land the wrong rating category` FALSE EQUALS `the complaint goes to` `no objection lies; a submission when rates are proposed (s 6.36)`
#ASSERT `Where does my complaint about my rates go to` `as the owner` `the rate record gives my land the wrong rating category` TRUE EQUALS `the complaint goes to` (`Where does my complaint go` `the rate record gives my land the wrong rating category` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Where does my complaint about my rates go to` `as the tenant` `an unasked complaint` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

#ASSERT `Is my objection to the rate record validly made` `as the owner` 42 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my objection to the rate record validly made` `as the owner` 43 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my objection to the rate record validly made` `as the owner` 50 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my objection validly made` 50 TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is my objection to the rate record validly made` `as the tenant` `an unasked number` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

